<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the "Loom Agents" desktop app (DEV-V5-38).

  Applied bundle-wide: Tauri signs every nested Mach-O (the loom-desktop app
  binary and the loom / fleet-db / node sidecars) with the entitlements file
  named by bundle.macOS.entitlements in tauri.conf.json, and release-macos.sh
  re-applies this same file in its defensive hardened re-sign.

  The load-bearing pair is for the embedded Node's V8 engine:
    - allow-jit: V8 maps MAP_JIT pages and flips them W^X for the JIT.
    - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: belt-and-suspenders for V8 code paths
      that write executable memory without the MAP_JIT dance.
  These were locked by the DEV-V5-31 native-addon audit, which proved the Flue
  node bundle + its dependency closure at the pinned commit contain no native
  (.node) addons, so we deliberately DO NOT grant
  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation (audit gate: if a native
  addon is ever introduced, revisit this file in the same change).

  Granting the JIT exceptions to the Go binaries too is harmless (they never
  JIT) and keeps the local and CI signing paths identical. get-task-allow is
  intentionally absent — the nodejs.org build ships it and the notary rejects
  it, so re-signing with this file (which omits it) strips it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
